\caption{The image on the left, plots the leading behaviour of the coefficients $2^k\, \delta_{\re} F^{(0,0)}_{2,k} \equiv - 2^{k}\,\mathrm{SF}_{(0\rightarrow1)} \times {\cal S}_{\re} \mathrm{BP}_{60} [\chi_{(0\rightarrow1)}] (k)$. In red we plot the original sequence, while in blue we plot its $\mathrm{RT}_{0,2} (0,k,5)$ Richardson transform. The purple line shows the constant value that this sequence is converging towards, $S_1^2 F_0^{(2,0)}= 1$. The image on the right, plots the leading behaviour of the coefficients $3^k\, \delta_{\im} F^{(0,0)}_{2,k} \equiv \im \left( F_k^{(0,0)}\, \frac{2\pi{\mathrm{i}} \left(3A\right)^k}{\Gamma(k)} \right) - 3^{k}\, \mathrm{SF}_{(0\rightarrow1)} \times {\cal S}_{\im} \mathrm{BP}_{60} [\chi_{(0\rightarrow1)}] (k)$, in red, and their first Richardson transform, in green. It is very clear how this sequence is converging towards a constant value of order $\sim {\cal O} (1)$, which immediately validates the expected $3^{-k}$ decay.}
